==Trivia==
*The Final Corpse's Japanese name, Saigo no Shisha (最後の屍者, "The Final Corpse"), is almost the same as [[Last of the Dead (Merciless)|Last of the Dead]]'s, with the only difference being that The Final Corpse spells ''Shisha'' (死者, dead person) as 屍者, replacing the kanji 死 (death) with 屍 (corpse). Both stages' names also sound identical to the Japanese title of ''[[Neon Genesis Evangelion Collaboration Event|Neon Genesis Evangelion]]'' [https://wiki.evageeks.org/Episode_24 Episode 24], except the episode's title spells ''Shisha'' as シ者, allowing it to be interpreted as either "The Final Dead Person" or "The Final Messenger"; this wordplay is used in [[Cruel Angel Clionel]]'s Japanese description as well.

